{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count of assignments to 12 variables satisfying CNF. Let's solve manually or use reasoning. Clauses list:\n\n1. [-9,1] => ¬x9 ∨ x1\n2. [-2,3] => ¬x2 ∨ x3\n3. [4,12] => x4 ∨ x12\n4. [-6,7] => ¬x6 ∨ x7\n5. [-5,1] => ¬x5 ∨ x1\n6. [-11,3] => ¬x11 ∨ x3\n7. [9,5] => x9 ∨ x5\n8. [6,10] => x6 ∨ x10\n9. [-10,7] => ¬x10 ∨ x7\n10. [11,2] => x11 ∨ x2\n11. [-4,8] => ¬x4 ∨ x8\n12. [-12,8] => ¬x12 ∨ x8\n\nWe need count of satisfying assignments. Let's analyze constraints.\n\nWe have variables 1-12.\n\nClauses pairwise:\n\nC1: ¬x9 ∨ x1  => if x9=1 then x1=1. Equivalent: x9 <= x1.\n\nC5: ¬x5 ∨ x1 => if x5=1 then x1=1. So x5 <= x1.\n\nC7: x9 ∨ x5 => at least one of x9,x5 is 1.\n\nThus combine: If x9=1 => x1=1. If x5=1 => x1=1. Also at least one of x9,x5 is 1. So possibilities: (x9=1,x5=0) or (x9=0,x5=1) or (x9=1,x5=1). In all cases x1 must be 1. So x1=1 forced. Good.\n\nThus x1=1.\n\nNow other clauses:\n\nC2: ¬x2 ∨ x3 => x2 <= x3.\n\nC6: ¬x11 ∨ x3 => x11 <= x3.\n\nC10: x11 ∨ x2 => at least one of x11,x2 is 1.\n\nSo we have x2 <= x3, x11 <= x3, and (x11 or x2)=1. So at least one of x2,x11 is 1. But both <= x3, so x3 must be 1 if either x2 or x11 is 1. Since at least one is 1, x3=1 forced. Then x2 and x11 can be 0 or 1 but must satisfy <= x3 (which is 1) so no restriction. So x3=1, x2,x11 free but at least one of them 1.\n\nNow clauses 3,4,8,9,11,12 involve x4,x6,x7,x8,x10,x12.\n\nC3: x4 ∨ x12 => at least one of x4,x12 is 1.\n\nC4: ¬x6 ∨ x7 => x6 <= x7.\n\nC8: x6 ∨ x10 => at least one of x6,x10 is 1.\n\nC9: ¬x10 ∨ x7 => x10 <= x7.\n\nC11: ¬x4 ∨ x8 => x4 <= x8.\n\nC12: ¬x12 ∨ x8 => x12 <= x8.\n\nAlso we have x8 appears in both"}}],"created":1790948319,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"pr